**Redesigning common functions for normalized coordinates**

I'm planning a thorough update of the common.py module to shift all relevant functions and patterns from millimeters to normalized coordinates. This includes refactoring build_particle, cartesian_to_polar, resolve_radius, and sample_uniform_disk_xy to handle normalized values consistently while keeping backward compatibility where practical. I'll introduce helpers for conversions between normalized and mm units, resolve radius and width from multiple config options, and unify type definitions. This foundation will support a smooth pattern update next. I'll likely rewrite common.py fully to keep changes clear and manageable.
