thinking
**Reworking particle finalization sequence**

I'm sorting out when to call `_finalize_particles` to ensure all particles, including background ones, have consistent and updated radius fields. Since jitter needs radius millimeters (r_mm), but also updates r_mm and normalized radius (r_norm), I think it’s best to remove the early finalization call and instead finalize only after adding background particles—this keeps fields correct without redundant processing. I’m also considering a helper to ensure r_mm exists pre-jitter, but jitter’s internal resolution seems sufficient, so I'll adjust the sample generation flow to finalize once, at the end.
