**Adding pattern validation checks in doctor run**

I’m planning to insert a new validation block right after the patterns loop in the doctor run, carefully limiting particle counts to avoid heavy computation. I’ll attempt loading the pattern catalog, then generate a small sample of particles per pattern to verify their normalized radius values stay within expected bounds while catching errors cleanly to report through doctor checks. I’ll also override n_particles in the sample context to keep tests lightweight and consider wafer radius from config or default. This should improve robustness of pattern validation without overwhelming the checks list.
